package "VEL Evidence Ingestion (S-CORE State Collection)" {

  package "Collector Hierarchy" {
    abstract class SourceCollector {
      +collector_id : string
      +source_ref : string
      +collection_trigger : CollectionTrigger
      +collection_window : object
      +parameters : object
      +collect() : Result<vector<RawStateRecord>, CollectorError>
      +get_metadata() : collection_metadata
      +get_diagnostics() : diagnostics
      +health_probe() : health_status
    }

    abstract class SCoreCollector {
      +source_ref : string = "score.<module>"
      +collector_id : string = "<module>-collector"
      +transport : Transport = s-core-api
    }

    class LifecycleCollector {
      +collector_id : string = "lifecycle-collector"
      +source_ref : string = "score.lifecycle"
    }

    SourceCollector <|-- SCoreCollector : extends
    SCoreCollector <|-- LifecycleCollector : extends

    note right of SourceCollector
      • Common VEL collector interface (all source categories)
      • I/O API per source-collector-interface-design.md Sec 3
      • Lifecycle state machine per Sec 4.1
      • Error taxonomy per Sec 5.1
    end note

    note right of SCoreCollector
      • S-CORE-specific conventions on top of SourceCollector
      • Naming: source_ref=score.<module>, collector_id=<module>-collector
      • Transport: s-core-api
      • See s-core-collector-common-design.md
    end note

    note right of LifecycleCollector
      • Concrete module collector for S-CORE Lifecycle
      • Inherits common I/O API + S-CORE conventions
      • source_ref=score.lifecycle, collector_id=lifecycle-collector
    end note
  }

  package "Shared Engine" {
    interface IStateFieldBindingProvider {
      +field_names() : list<string>
      +read_field(field_name : string) : any
      +subscribe(on_update : callback) : bool
    }

    class ConfigDrivenStateMapper {
      -schema_ref : RawEvidenceSchema
      +map_to_raw_record(bindings : IStateFieldBindingProvider) : object
      +validate_required_fields() : bool
    }

    class CollectorDiagnostics {
      +error_code : string
      +error_category : ErrorCategory
      +severity : Severity
      +message : string
      +retry_count : uint32
      +recovery_hint : string
      +emit() : AdapterDiagnostic
    }

    LifecycleCollector ..> IStateFieldBindingProvider : uses (as LifecycleFieldBindings)
    LifecycleCollector ..> ConfigDrivenStateMapper : uses
    LifecycleCollector ..> CollectorDiagnostics : reports via
    ConfigDrivenStateMapper ..> IStateFieldBindingProvider : reads fields via

    note right of IStateFieldBindingProvider
      • Generic engine classes shown here in collapsed form;
        see the dedicated common diagram for full notes on
        why these are SHARED (not Lifecycle-specific):
        [Collector_common_class_diagram.puml]
      • This diagram shows only the Lifecycle-specific
        REALIZATION: LifecycleFieldBindings implementing
        this interface (below)
    end note
  }

  package "Lifecycle-Specific Adapter (the only new code for this module)" {
    class LifecycleFieldBindings {
      -transport : s-core-api = lifecycle-state-api
      +field_names() : list<string>
      +read_field(field_name : string) : any
      +subscribe(on_update : callback) : bool
    }

    IStateFieldBindingProvider <|.. LifecycleFieldBindings : implements

    note right of LifecycleFieldBindings
      • Thin adapter: field_name -> S-CORE API call. It maintains
        TWO mw::com service connections:
        (1) ILmControl (pull) for run_target via
            get_active_run_target()
        (2) IExtMonitorNotify (push) for all other fields via
            ext_monitor_notify callback
      • ProcessInfoNode and Graph (state/pid/graph_state) are
        INTERNAL Launch Manager daemon classes -- NOT reachable by
        an external VEL process and NOT part of ILmControl (see
        note on ProcessInfoNode below)
      • state, pid, graph_state, exit_code, process_execution_error,
        supervision_status, failed_supervision_type,
        failed_supervision_cycles, deadline_error, heartbeat_error,
        logic_error, deadline_violation, alive_indication_count,
        process_group_id, recovery_state -- all delivered via the
        external monitor notification capability
        (comp_req__launch_man__ext_monitor_notify) as a
        ProcessMonitorNotify payload, through IExtMonitorNotify
      • read_field(): pull-based read for run_target only
      • subscribe(): registers a callback against the external monitor
        notification capability and returns true once that
        registration succeeds (false if this source has no
        event-driven path available); on each callback invocation the
        adapter builds one immutable snapshot of the full payload
        (originating from PHM via LM) and atomically swaps it in;
        read_field() calls within one collection cycle all resolve
        against that same snapshot, never mixing two event generations
      • Implements IStateFieldBindingProvider only -- does NOT
        duplicate ConfigDrivenStateMapper or CollectorDiagnostics
      • This is the ONLY class a future module needs to write
        beyond its schema/mapping/collector config
    end note
  }

  package "Enums" {
    enum CollectionTrigger {
      PERIODIC
      EVENT
      ON_DEMAND
    }

    enum Transport {
      S_CORE_API
      DDS
      FILE
      COMMAND
      OS_INTERFACE
    }

    enum ErrorCategory {
      CONFIGURATION_ERROR
      SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
      AUTHENTICATION_ERROR
      TIMEOUT
      SCHEMA_VIOLATION
      NORMALIZATION_ERROR
      RESOURCE_EXHAUSTION
      INTERNAL_ERROR
    }

    enum Severity {
      INFO
      WARNING
      ERROR
      FATAL
    }

    enum CollectorLifecycleState {
      PROVISIONED
      ACTIVE
      RUNNING
      SUSPENDED
      ERROR
      TERMINATED
    }

    SourceCollector --> CollectionTrigger : collection_trigger
    SourceCollector --> CollectorLifecycleState : lifecycle state
    SCoreCollector --> Transport : transport
    CollectorDiagnostics --> ErrorCategory : error_category
    CollectorDiagnostics --> Severity : severity
  }
}

package "S-CORE Lifecycle (source-side types)" {
  enum ProcessState {
    kIdle = 0
    kStarting = 1
    kRunning = 2
    kTerminating = 3
    kTerminated = 4
    kFailed = 5
  }

  enum GraphState {
    kSuccess = 0
    kInTransition = 1
    kAborting = 2
    kCancelled = 3
    kUndefinedState = 4
  }

  enum SupervisionStatus {
    kOk = 0
    kFailed = 1
  }

  enum FailedSupervisionType {
    kHeartbeat = 0
    kDeadline = 1
    kLogic = 2
  }

  enum DeadlineError {
    kTooEarly = 0
    kTooLate = 1
  }

  enum HeartbeatError {
    kTooEarly = 0
    kTooLate = 1
    kMultipleHeartbeats = 2
  }

  enum LogicError {
    kInvalidState = 0
    kInvalidTransition = 1
    kUnmappedError = 2
  }

  class ProcessInfoNode {
    +getPid() : osal::ProcessID
    +getState() : ProcessState
    +getTerminationTimeout() : milliseconds
    +getControlClientChannel() : ControlClientChannelP
  }

  note right of ProcessInfoNode
    • INTERNAL class of the Launch Manager daemon
      (score::mw::lifecycle::internal, process_group_manager/details/)
    • NOT part of the public ILmControl interface, NOT exposed via
      mw::com, and NOT reachable by an external VEL process
    • Shown here ONLY to document the origin/type of state and pid --
      VEL does NOT call these getters directly
  end note

  interface ILmControl {
    +get_active_run_target() : RunTargetName
  }

  interface IExtMonitorNotify {
    +subscribe(on_notify : callback) : Result<void>
    +latest() : optional<ProcessMonitorNotify>
  }

  class ProcessMonitorNotify {
    +process_name : string
    +process_group_name : string
    +process_state : ProcessState
    +pid : uint32
    +exit_code : int32
    +supervision_status : SupervisionStatus
    +failed_supervision_type : FailedSupervisionType
    +deadline_error : DeadlineError
    +deadline_error_us : int64
    +heartbeat_error : HeartbeatError
    +logic_error : LogicError
    +failed_supervision_cycles : uint32
    +deadline_violation : bool
    +alive_indication_count : uint32
    +process_execution_error : uint32
    +process_group_id : string
    +recovery_state : string
  }

  note right of ProcessMonitorNotify
    • Payload type delivered by the external monitor notification
      capability (score::mw::lifecycle::ProcessMonitorNotify)
    • process_name/process_group_name identify WHICH process a given
      notification is about: the callback is registered ONCE per
      LifecycleFieldBindings instance (not once per process), so each
      notification must self-identify its subject for the adapter to
      route it to the correct resource_id
    • Originates from Platform Health Monitor (PHM) for the fields PHM
      evaluates; delivered to LifecycleFieldBindings via Launch
      Manager's external monitor notification capability
    • Delivered via the IExtMonitorNotify mw::com event service
  end note

  ProcessInfoNode --> ProcessState : getState()
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> SupervisionStatus : supervision_status
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> FailedSupervisionType : failed_supervision_type
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> DeadlineError : deadline_error
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> HeartbeatError : heartbeat_error
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> LogicError : logic_error
}

LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ProcessState : reads (type only, via notification)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> GraphState : reads (type only, via notification)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ProcessMonitorNotify : reads via notification
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ILmControl : pull (run_target via get_active_run_target)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> IExtMonitorNotify : push (subscribe for ProcessMonitorNotify)

note bottom of LifecycleFieldBindings
  • Pull field (synchronous, stable, public API): ONLY
    run_target, via ILmControl::get_active_run_target()
  • state, pid, graph_state are NOT accessible via any public getter --
    ProcessInfoNode::getState()/getPid() and Graph's state accessor are
    INTERNAL Launch Manager daemon classes, not reachable cross-process
    and not exposed through ILmControl
  • All push fields (state, pid, graph_state, exit_code,
    process_execution_error, supervision_status,
    failed_supervision_type, deadline_error, heartbeat_error,
    logic_error, deadline_violation, failed_supervision_cycles,
    alive_indication_count, process_group_id, recovery_state) are
    delivered via the IExtMonitorNotify mw::com event service as a
    ProcessMonitorNotify payload
  • See lifecycle-collector-design.md Sec 2.4 and Sec 6 for the full
    accessibility boundary
end note

@enduml